**Issue**: #369
**Date**: 2026-09-06
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Progress-bounded execute remediation and owned cancellation
  As an operator running execute
  I want autonomous repairs to advance the pipeline and cancellation to stop owned work
  So that a failed stage cannot consume unbounded work

  @AC1
  Scenario: Start one repair before checking its outcome
    Given an incomplete remediable step has a settled failed non-intervention handoff
    When execute continues
    Then it starts one remediation worker
    And it observes that worker before starting another

  @AC2
  Scenario: Stop after two unsuccessful remediations
    Given two remediations have finished for the same issue and step
    And currentStep and completed have not advanced
    When execute would otherwise start another remediation
    Then it records remediation_loop and stopped remediation
    And it closes controller-owned worker panes
    And it starts no third remediation
    And reinvocation with unchanged evidence remains stopped

  @AC3
  Scenario Outline: Preserve a genuine stop across resume
    Given a settled handoff has status <status> and intervention <intervention>
    When execute observes it and is subsequently reinvoked unchanged
    Then it starts no remediation worker
    And it does not reinterpret that handoff as permission to rewind

    Examples:
      | status  | intervention |
      | blocked | false        |
      | failed  | true         |
      | passed  | true         |

  @AC4
  Scenario: Continue after repaired success
    Given a remediation finishes with a valid passed non-intervention handoff
    When execute records that step in completed
    Then it advances currentStep and clears the no-progress streak
    And it continues the remaining pipeline

  @AC5
  Scenario Outline: Apply progress detection to every remediable stage
    Given the current step is <step>
    And two remediation workers finish without advancing the step
    When execute checks progress
    Then it stops with remediation_loop before starting a third repair

    Examples:
      | step      |
      | implement |
      | review1   |
      | fix1      |
      | review2   |
      | fix2      |
      | verify    |
      | deliver   |

  @AC6
  Scenario Outline: Cancel while an external wait blocks the controller
    Given execute owns a worker pane and is blocked in an external command
    And retain-worker was not passed
    When cancellation occurs through <source>
    Then the owned controller process group stops
    And the owned worker pane closes
    And the latest run checkpoint records controller_cancelled
    And unrelated worker panes remain untouched

    Examples:
      | source             |
      | SIGINT             |
      | SIGTERM            |
      | invoking job death |

  @AC6
  Scenario: Cleanup includes a worker whose prompt has not activated
    Given execute owns a pending or activating worker pane
    When execute is cancelled
    Then it closes that pane and records cancellation

  @AC7
  Scenario: Retain a worker explicitly
    Given execute was invoked with retain-worker
    When it stops or is cancelled
    Then its owned worker pane remains open
    And the stopped or cancelled checkpoint remains recorded

  @AC8
  Scenario: Bound smoke verification to the plugin change
    Given an exercise targets a named nmg-sdlc defect
    When the smoke repository exposes an unrelated application failure or repeats unchanged evidence
    Then the operator records the failure without repairing unrelated smoke code
    And another run requires a concrete changed hypothesis or plugin repair
    And steering permits smoke edits only as necessary verification fixtures

  @AC9
  Scenario: Follow the complete operating guide
    Given a user installs or updates the plugin
    When they follow README.md
    Then documented commands cover setup through exact-head merge and issue closure
    And recovery and smoke boundaries match the runtime and registered steering
    And the implementation has been reviewed against main before delivery

  @AC4
  Scenario: Resume verified delivery after a loop stop
    Given delivery stopped with remediation_loop and no live worker
    And a subsequently validated passed delivery handoff proves the exact merged head and closed issue
    When execute resumes
    Then it completes the existing delivery verification and checkout cleanup
    And it launches no replacement remediation

  @AC10
  Scenario: Clean descendants after direct controller loss
    Given execute owns a blocking external descendant
    And that descendant holds inherited output pipes
    And an unrelated process group is running
    When the controller leader is killed directly
    Then waiting ends and the owned descendant is terminated before ownership is released
    And the checkpoint records controller_process_lost
    And the unrelated group remains alive

  @AC10
  Scenario Outline: End supervised waiting after leader loss
    Given an owned <consumer> command has a descendant holding its output pipes
    When the command leader disappears before a valid terminal result
    Then the remaining owned group is cleaned up
    And the result remains failed or incomplete rather than passed
    And unrelated processes are untouched

    Examples:
      | consumer            |
      | verification        |
      | smoke verification  |
      | OMP exercise        |

  @AC10
  Scenario: Preserve usage failures through the supervisor
    Given execute is invoked with an unknown argument
    When the public CLI rejects the invocation
    Then it exits with usage status 2
    And it creates no worker or controller lease

  @AC10
  Scenario: Preserve ordinary closed-process cleanup safety
    Given normal cleanup observes an already-closed child
    When its old process identity could have been reused
    Then ordinary cleanup sends no signal to that identity
    And only freshly observed owned leader loss can use explicit descendant cleanup

  @AC11
  Scenario: Consume canonical implicit scenario identities
    Given an approved implicit single-issue spec has untagged scenarios
    And its verification report contains the exact scope resolver output
    When readiness validates the report
    Then canonical named scenario identities are accepted
    And stale, duplicate, malformed, or explicit-manifest named identities are rejected

  @AC11
  Scenario: Repair local report evidence without waiving verification
    Given the current safe verification report has an unverifiable local format
    When finalization evaluates it
    Then it emits an unpassed non-intervention handoff with the report artifact
    And bounded verification remediation can regenerate the report
    And publication and advancement require a subsequently validated report
    And unsafe paths or genuinely incomplete external evidence remain intervention conditions

  @AC6
  Scenario: Survive complete invoking-job tree cancellation
    Given the invocation bootstrap has exited and the supervisor is reparented
    And execute owns a live worker
    When the harness kills the complete invoking-job process tree
    Then the surviving supervisor observes authenticated connection loss
    And it closes the owned worker and records controller_cancelled before releasing its lease
    And unrelated review workers remain alive

  @AC11
  Scenario: Recheck live scope before publication and delivery
    Given a same-issue verification marker omits a current canonical obligation
    When finalization or delivery rechecks the live spec
    Then the stale marker is rejected before protected mutation
    And no passed handoff or delivery progression is produced
